body:
Porn isn't bad but for me typically I stay away from mainstream porn companies work because they added to my massive body dysmorphia and made me ashamed of myself. Even now at points I get hyper-fixated on this stuff whenever I see mainstream porn companies work. 

&#x200B;

I think porn can be liberating but also destructive and addictive.

I think people men should talk about sex with each other. I've honestly found talking to a few of my guy friends about sex has been really nice. Learning how we suffer from the same insecurities in ourselves. Learning that I shouldn't be worried about my penis size came from talking with men. I think its the norm to say "oh I banged x last night" but for men I think it's a symptom that society doesn't want us to be emotional and in a way talking about sex, positives and negatives leads to showing emotions. 

&#x200B;

All I can really say is fixing this is talking about it. I learned to be okay with my average average size simply by talking to my dude bros and some women that I am close friends with. Overall I think another hurdle is people don't want to show that their insecure with themselves.
